      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To differentiate between oxidized and reduced firing atmospheres, look at the surface color and behavior of the clay body. Oxidized firing tends to produce copper or turquoise-like colors, often with a green or greenish-yellow patina, whereas reduced firing tends to produce blue, gray, or black colors. Additionally, reduced-firing ceramics can exhibit a more subtle, glassy sheen, whereas oxidized ceramics may appear more matte or brushed. Consider the overall appearance and sheen of the surfaces, as well as any subtle color gradations or warm/cool undertones.",
